# Changelog

All notable changes to A.G.N.E.S. (Adaptive Grid Neural Engineering System) are documented in this file.

# v4.2 (2026-03-28)

# Added
- CUSUM sequential change detection on rolling Brier score and rolling confidence streams
- Page Hinkley sequential change detection as a complementary gradual drift detector
- Triple signal drift detection figure (PSI, CUSUM, Page Hinkley side by side)
- First alert batch logging for all three detectors in streaming summary
- CPCV configuration flags (use_cpcv, cpcv_purge_batches, cpcv_embargo_batches) for deployment readiness on temporal data
- Governance metadata block with monitoring metrics list, recalibration triggers, and auditability records
- SHAP stability under drift analysis (feature rankings verified across clean, gradual, and abrupt phases)
- Cross regime validation (train on one operating regime, test on another)
- Synthetic DSGC data generation with physics derived labels for out of distribution testing
- Feature space PSI and KL divergence computed per batch against training distributions
- Inference latency benchmarking (single sample and batch throughput)
- 19 publication quality figures generated automatically at 300 DPI
- ROC curves, precision recall curves, confusion matrix heatmaps, and feature correlation matrix figures

# Changed
- Renamed from A.N.E. (Atlas Nexus Engine) to A.G.N.E.S. (Adaptive Grid Neural Engineering System)
- Streaming simulation now includes confidence_mean per batch for CUSUM monitoring
- Streaming summary JSON includes drift_signals block with all detector results
- All display text cleaned to pure ASCII (no Unicode decorative characters)
- Console output uses clean ASCII formatting throughout

# v4.1 (2026-03-16)

# Added
- Three layer streaming deployment simulation (concept drift + regime change + SCADA corruption)
- Gradual tau drift simulating aging inverters with increasing reaction times
- Abrupt gamma shift simulating sudden network reconfiguration
- SCADA corruption layer: Gaussian sensor noise, ADC quantisation, missing values, measurement latency
- Rolling window metrics (AUC, ECE, Brier, coverage) across 120 streaming batches
- Phase summaries (pre drift, gradual, post abrupt) for all four models
- Conformal coverage tracking under drift conditions
- PSI based recalibration alert system with configurable threshold
- Browser export (JSON model bundle for web deployment)
- Auto stabiliser using Adam optimiser for corrective grid control actions

# Changed
- Expanded stress testing to run all four models (previously only Hybrid)
- Monte Carlo noise testing now covers SVM, RF, and LGBM alongside Hybrid

# v4.0 (2026-03-10)

# Added
- RFECV feature selection (48 engineered features reduced to 14)
- Physics informed feature engineering v4: F_gain (feedback gain), H_net (network heterogeneity), V_weak (worst case vulnerability)
- Cost optimal threshold selection with configurable cost matrix (FN cost = 10, FP cost = 1)
- Three level risk index (STABLE, BORDERLINE, CRITICAL) with data driven boundaries
- Conformal prediction with split conformal method and finite sample correction
- Paired bootstrap AUC significance test (2000 resamples)
- Learning curve analysis (AUC vs training size for all models)
- FGSM adversarial robustness testing at six epsilon levels across all models
- Calibration drift analysis under noise and OOD stress
- Stage wise checkpoints for crash recovery (checkpoint_hpo.joblib, checkpoint_models.joblib)

# Changed
- Feature pipeline expanded from 24 to 48 candidates before RFECV selection
- Evaluation suite expanded with Brier score, ECE, PR AUC, log loss alongside existing AUC and F1
- Permutation importance now uses 5 repeats for stability

# v3.0 (2026-02-20)

# Added
- Stacking hybrid ensemble (SVM + RF base learners with logistic meta learner)
- Calibrated probability outputs via Platt scaling (SVM) and isotonic regression (RF, LGBM)
- Bayesian hyperparameter optimisation via Optuna with TPE sampler
- Parallel HPO mode (concurrent SVM, RF, LGBM searches via ThreadPoolExecutor)
- SHAP explainability with TreeExplainer on RF and LGBM including interaction values
- Full stress testing suite: Gaussian noise injection, OOD scaling, boundary sensitivity, Monte Carlo
- Physics informed features v3: D_eff (effective damping), R (responsiveness), delta_g (elasticity deviation)
- Cross validated evaluation (5 fold stratified)

# Changed
- Moved from single model evaluation to four model comparison (SVM, RF, LightGBM, Logistic Regression)
- Added validation split for calibration (60/20/20 train/val/test)
- Parallelism enforced to single layer to prevent thread oversubscription

# v2.0 (2026-01-25)

# Added
- SVM with RBF kernel and probability estimates
- Random Forest classifier with balanced class weights
- LightGBM with early stopping
- Basic feature engineering: per node D_eff and R features
- Aggregate statistics: tau_mean, tau_std, g_mean, g_std, p_imbalance
- Stratified train/test split
- AUC and F1 evaluation metrics

# Changed
- Migrated from notebook based workflow to single script pipeline
- Structured output to artifacts directory

# v1.0 (2025-12-15)

# Added
- Initial exploratory analysis of UCI Smart Grid Stability dataset
- Logistic Regression baseline
- Basic accuracy evaluation
- Data loading and preprocessing
